## Closing Statement

The Council protocol demonstrates strong foundational design: clear phase structure, well-defined artifacts, disciplined escalation mechanics, honest acknowledgment of current limitations (fallback mode, draft status).

Primary architectural risk identified by all three roles: **scaling assumptions baked into MVP-era decisions** — fixed role sets, flat-file concurrency, completely stateless sessions, naive context propagation, manual moderation. Addressing these proactively starting with the P0 package will keep Council viable through Phases 2, 3, and beyond.

No recommended improvement contradicts core principles in `project-concept.md`. They extend MVP minimalism into structural resilience, preserving: *whatever is not hard to implement in code is done in code; everything else is delegated to AI.*

